# The reference room (see docs/rendering/reference-scenes.md): Blender's reference.blend, a closed box 4 m square and
# 21.4 m long with walls 5.8 cm thick, lit only by a sun through a window of 2 m in its west wall, under a black sky. The
# sun is level, so it lights a patch of the blue end wall and the east wall's corner, and everything else is its bounced
# light. Cycles' render of it from the camera here, with the same lens and no depth of field, is
# samples/mygame/reference/room/reference.png; tools/refdiff compares the Game view's screenshot with it. Blender's +z is
# this scene's +y, and its +y this scene's -z, as the glTF exporter and the cooker's mirror of x leave it. Positions are
# raw World_Position values in units of 2^-24 m. The editor writes this file; see docs/editor/document-and-scenes.md#scenes.
